  "Evidence says little: every non-label mesh is one or five equal-extent solids (size 0.1 on each axis, 1280 triangles each, no uv/colour). Nothing in position/size/colour tells what they are, so they are named by shape (Equal_Extent_Solid) plus the material family word from the material name (material names are evidence but not listed in basis): Spec/White/Yellow/Hdr, Factor vs Texture, and the ordinal from the material suffix written as a word.",
  "Rule used: mesh with material M<n>.<k>_<family>Fac -> one whole part '<Family>_Factor_Equal_Extent_Solid_<k as word>'. Mesh with a *Tex material -> five islands, one part each, named by x position (at.x .91 Far_Right, .70 Right_Middle, .50 Centre, .30 Left_Middle, .09 Far_Left); the five islands are in a row along x. Left/right is assumed to follow at.x low = left.",
